<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil firms.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil firms.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5387) DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS     LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     40.90/41.30     26.58/26.84     40.10/40.50</p>
<p> BREMEN		40.90/41.30     26.58/26.84     40.10/40.50</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    41.20/41.60     26.77/27.03     40.40/40.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   42.65/43.15     27.72/28.04     41.80/42.20</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   42.65/43.15     27.72/28.04     42.00/42.40</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  43.85/44.25     24.89/28.75     43.20/43.60</p>
<p>German inland gas oil gained in quiet trade on Wednesday on the back of firmer IPE futures. End-users remained virtually absent from the market in hope of lower prices and because of unusually temperate weather. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
